Texture parking keeps more headroom and reports what the device leaves and how often it presents (Minato, patch 0018).

Why: on an iPhone 15 Pro Max a visual novel's frame sequence held at 4.6-5.2 GB of a ~6 GB limit with patch 0017,
alive for the whole run but with a memory warning nearly every 2 s: 0017 started parking below 1 GiB available, where
the device already warns (from about 5.0 GB on in the run without parking). Parking now starts below 1.5 GiB and stops
at 2 GiB (ADR-0075's 512 MiB hysteresis kept); a cycled sequence costs the same restores per shown frame either way.
ANGLEMetalParkingLine gains " avail_min=<MiB> avail_last=<MiB> present_p50=<ms> present_p99=<ms>": the least and the
last memory the process could still allocate at a frame end (0 when unknown), and the time between the last 512
presents of a window, so that a device run shows the headroom and the frame rate the restores leave.
Test: graphics/tests/angle_texture_parking.mm presents through a window surface now (ANGLE presents only a window
drawn into since its last swap): the line's fields, the presents' interval at 1/60 s; --warning-band measures the
least memory left with a device-like limit.
Upstream: no (Minato's memory policy).
